scope: |
  `String.length` answered BYTES on the Rust lane while substring/charAt index UTF-16 code units —
  LANDED 808b8fd0e, CI in flight. Widened to the defect the same reporter is blocked by next:
  a handler written as an inline lambda, or in the block form `route(m, p) { h }`, is typed as a
  STRING handler — `handlerDeclaresRequest` only recognises an annotated parameter or a call to a
  def, and the block form does not even reach it (`argTerms.size == 3` is false for a curried
  apply). Measured: no spelling of `route` works on all three lanes today.
